<section class="section border-t border-ink-primary" aria-labelledby="oracle-case-heading"><div class="wrapper grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-4"><p class="meta reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-orange)">The assignment</span></p><h2 id="oracle-case-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">The ERP should clarify the business, not complicate it.</h2></div><div class="oracle-case-copy col-span-12 md:col-span-7"><p class="oracle-case-lead text-xl md:text-2xl text-ink-secondary reveal">When systems, data, and handoffs pull in different directions, finance spends too much of its time reconciling the past. We design Oracle Cloud ERP around the decisions and operations that move the business forward.</p><div class="oracle-outcomes reveal reveal-delay-2"><div><span>Less reconciliation</span><p>Reliable flows and validation across core processes.</p></div><div><span>More visibility</span><p>Reporting built for decisions, not spreadsheet assembly.</p></div><div><span>Room to grow</span><p>A standard-first foundation that can absorb change.</p></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="section section-statement" aria-labelledby="oracle-services-heading"><div class="wrapper grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-4"><p class="meta text-ink-inverse-secondary reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-yellow)">What we own</span></p><h2 id="oracle-services-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">From the first decision to the next release.</h2><p class="mt-6 text-ink-inverse-secondary max-w-md reveal reveal-delay-1">Bring us in for a defined workstream, or let us connect the whole transformation.</p></div><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-8 md:pl-8"><ol class="oracle-services"><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><span>01</span><div><h3>Advisory &amp; architecture</h3><p>Readiness, fit-gap, process design, target architecture, data and integration strategy, plus a transformation plan people can execute.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-2"><span>02</span><div><h3>Fusion Cloud implementation</h3><p>Configuration across financials, procurement, projects, and performance management with security, workflows, reporting, enablement, and cutover built in.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-3"><span>03</span><div><h3>Migration &amp; data confidence</h3><p>Legacy assessment, data profiling and cleansing, mapping, mock loads, reconciliation, and production migration without treating data as an afterthought.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-4"><span>04</span><div><h3>Integration, automation &amp; insight</h3><p>Oracle Integration Cloud, APIs, exception paths, automated workflows, and reporting that connects ERP to the rest of the enterprise.</p></div></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><span>05</span><div><h3>Quality &amp; continuous operations</h3><p>End-to-end testing, release assurance, hypercare, quarterly release support, and practical improvements once the system is live.</p></div></li></ol></div></div></section>

<section id="engagement" class="oracle-engagement section border-t border-ink-primary" aria-labelledby="oracle-path-heading"><div class="wrapper"><div class="grid-edit"><div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5"><p class="meta reveal"><span class="section-number" style="--accent:var(--color-pixel-green)">Delivery path</span></p><h2 id="oracle-path-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.03em] mt-6 reveal">A clear sequence. No theatre.</h2></div><div class="oracle-path-copy col-span-12 md:col-span-6"><p class="text-lg text-ink-secondary reveal">The exact shape depends on your estate. The order does not: establish the facts, design decisions early, validate hard, then stay accountable beyond go-live.</p></div></div><ol class="oracle-path"><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><b>01</b><h3>Discover</h3><p>Objectives, processes, applications, integrations, data, and constraints.</p></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-2"><b>02</b><h3>Design</h3><p>Future-state process, architecture, controls, and delivery plan.</p></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-3"><b>03</b><h3>Build</h3><p>Configure, integrate, migrate, and prepare business teams.</p></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-4"><b>04</b><h3>Prove</h3><p>Test the workflows, data, reporting, security, and cutover.</p></li><li class="reveal reveal-delay-1"><b>05</b><h3>Operate</h3><p>Go-live, hypercare, releases, enhancements, and optimization.</p></li></ol></div></section>

